     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>recently, when I used plyr to convert some data, I got a whole column of NA values.</div><div>For simplicity, I make a toy test code to demonstrate what I encountered:</div><div>###########################################################################################</div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><div><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:14px;line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap;border-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;outline:none;border-style:none;line-height:1.2;font-size:10.4pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"color:blue\">&gt; acc &lt;- c(1.1, 1.2, 1.3, 2.1, 2.2, 2.3, 3.1, 3.2, 3.3)</span></pre></span></div></div><div><div><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:14px;line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap;border-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;outline:none;border-style:none;line-height:1.2;font-size:10.4pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"color:blue\">&gt; ds &lt;- rep(letters[1:3], each=3)</span></pre></span></div></div><div><div><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:14px;line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap;border-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;outline:none;border-style:none;line-height:1.2;font-size:10.4pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"color:blue\">&gt; r &lt;- data.frame(ds, acc)</span></pre></span></div></div><div><div><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:14px;line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap;border-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\